the boot file and the floppy drive as the boot location.
3.  I've created an MSDOS Milo boot disk with linload.exe and the Avanti
Milo image.

My plan was to load the generic.gz kernel image from the Linux CD after I
boot into Milo.

Currently the boot disk allows me to successfully boot into Milo.  At the
Milo prompt I issue the following commands:
show (to initialize the CDROM device)
boot sr0:kernels/generic.gz root=/dev/scd0

