jacket. So, I'm out in the extreme tail anyhow.. it only makes sense that
my machines look weird.  :)

> Yeah, but I guess I see machines differently.  I don't care how they look
> as look as they fill the requirements and are within my price range.

Indeed. Ultimately I am in the same category -- I tack on decoration as an
afterthought, really -- but for the people who treat computers like home
appliances, they'll buy a CD deck that matches the rest of their stereo..

In my mind it is a decent strategy by Apple: their market is a niche
Mac-lover market to begin with, highly individualist by nature, so they
are preserving the share that they have, and maybe make some waves and
get new customers: we are both talking about buying one. 

Plus, this is how Apple operates; they aim to the individual. Remember
their Big Brother ad? "Think different." .. thats their gimmick. Whether
it is enough to sell machines or not is another question, personally,
were I Apple, I'd take my own advice and "Think different" .. but hey..
who the hell am I .. I'm just a poor college kid with tatoos .. :)


