as I can:

hdparm -c1d1m16X34u1k1K1 /dev/hda 

On an IBM 15gig (U)DMA hard drive. Here are some common results for
hdparm -vTt /dev/hda:

/dev/hda:
 multcount    = 16 (on)
 I/O support  =  1 (32-bit)
 unmaskirq    =  1 (on)
 using_dma    =  1 (on)
 keepsettings =  1 (on)
 nowerr       =  0 (off)
 readonly     =  0 (off)
