With regards to your message at 09:57 AM 1/18/00 -0500, Kid. Where you stated:

>I messed up and bought Tin RAM for my gold-socketed Multia.  I want to put
>the RAM in but am afraid of what might happen....  I saw some posts about
>gold-vs-tin plating and know that I would be on "borrowed time" before
>weird things happened.  But what are those things?  Does some buildup crop
>up that I can easily get rid of or am I looking at permanent damage?
It may or may not be a problem. Generally it takes a fairly high humidity 
level for the damage to occur.
Also tin in Gold sockets seems to be less failure prone than the opposite 
in my experience..


